cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Latent Geometry vs. Prediction Error: a pre-registered, leakage-free
  early-warning benchmark for video world models
message: If you use this harness or benchmark, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TODO: add author(s) before release"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered evaluation harness testing whether the internal
  representation geometry of a frozen video world model signals sudden
  physical or visual anomalies earlier than the model's own prediction error.
  Provides a synthetic anomaly benchmark, three online geometry probes, two
  prediction-error baselines (including the model's own pretraining objective
  evaluated causally), survival analysis of time-to-detection, and a
  model-agnostic adapter contract enforced by a parameterised test suite.
keywords:
  - world models
  - anomaly detection
  - V-JEPA
  - survival analysis
  - pre-registration
  - representation geometry
license: MIT
